<p>President Trump said the United States would begin “Project Freedom” on Monday morning Middle East time to guide ships out of the Strait of Hormuz, where Iran has restricted traffic during the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran. He described the effort as assistance for countries not involved in the conflict and said U.S. representatives were talking with Iran, but gave few details on how the operation would work. Iran rejected the plan. Ebrahim Azizi, head of the Iranian parliament’s national security commission, said any U.S. interference in what Tehran calls the new maritime regime for the strait would violate the ceasefire. Iran’s military later warned it would attack foreign armed forces, especially U.S. forces, if they entered or approached the Strait of Hormuz, and told commercial ships to coordinate any movement with Iranian forces. The announcement followed reports of attacks around the waterway. In one incident, unknown projectiles hit a tanker near the Strait of Hormuz; UK Maritime Trade Operations said the incident occurred about 78 nautical miles north of Fujairah and that all crew were safe. Iran’s restrictions began after the United States and Israel launched the war on Feb. 28, and talks have remained deadlocked since a ceasefire took effect on April 8.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/pcs1vSVAKa_sdwIbjCbSuXKhSiJmbC4e-ub9FbEY2a0qSGDDHY1BMo8fZ2Y3cty2LpekfqvQ3yBXH4MWeKvgUmtmSuWV0mrPrwDhY4bglmKvphod2Pfw4rXnSbSY13kYeoDQ-Lcgq3wSjhDuhZdmCQfGjjAZFheXD6DzKv916XKX5bWfClQADMUD1YdHOBpXKXdDin5FfQoi_ZOesHA' alt='A man stands in the water as bulk carriers, cargo ships and service vessels line the horizon in the Strait of Hormuz off Bandar Abbas, Iran, on April 27, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Military scale: U.S. Central Command said the mission would involve guided-missile destroyers, more than 100 aircraft and 15,000 service members, though the Pentagon did not immediately explain how they would be deployed.</li><li>U.S. warning: Trump said any interference with what he called a humanitarian process would “have to be dealt with forcefully”.</li></ul><blockquote>The Strait of Hormuz and the Persian Gulf will not be governed by Trump’s delusional statements - Ebrahim Azizi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: Trump said a new Iranian proposal was likely unacceptable because Tehran had not “paid a big enough price,” and later described contacts with Iran as positive. (<a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/05/03/trump-free-ships-strait-of-hormuz-00904160'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Iranian parliament national security commission: Ebrahim Azizi rejected Washington’s description of Project Freedom as assistance for uninvolved countries, saying the waterway would remain subject to Iranian-defined rules. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/iran-warns-of-ceasefire-violation-as-us-plans-to-escort-hormuz-ships/article70937369.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iranian military command: The command accused the United States of “piracy” and of risking the world economy, and said Iran would respond harshly to threats or attacks. (<a href='https://www.birgun.net/haber/irandan-abdye-hurmuz-bogazi-uyarisi-710123'>Birgun</a>)</li><li>U.S. Central Command: CENTCOM said U.S. support for the mission was defensive and essential for regional security and the global economy. (<a href='https://www.lasexta.com/noticias/internacional/iran-advierte-trump-que-cualquier-interferencia-ormuz-sera-considerada-violacion-alto-fuego_2026050469f832616a56d80bba7e8a6e.html'>La Sexta</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3352291/cargo-ship-near-strait-hormuz-reports-being-attacked-iran-makes-new-peace-proposal'>Trump says US will ‘guide’ ships out of Hormuz, as vessels attacked</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-trump-strait-of-hormuz-israel-lebanon-ceasefire/'>Trump announces effort to guide ships out of Strai